In order to resolve the "nat" version issue when installing flycircuit, I downloaded the flycircuit tarball <https://github.com/jefferis/flycircuit/tarball/master>, found the DESCRIPTION file changed the requirement from 1.8.8 to 1.8.6, then ran R CMD INSTALL to get it to install, and it is fine now, in that I am able to install flycircuit data. Probably should fix it in the github if 1.8.6 is in fact the latest version.

However, when I run Shiny according to the instructions:
library(shiny)
runGitHub("jefferislab/NBLAST_on-the-fly")
